PythonJavaScriptcurl <pre><code>from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(base_url="http://localhost:9000/v1", api_key="your-api-key")

with open("audio.mp3", "rb") as audio:
    transcript = client.audio.transcriptions.create(model="whisper-1", file=audio)
print(transcript.text)
</code></pre> <pre><code>import fs from "fs";
import OpenAI from "openai";

const client = new OpenAI({ baseURL: "http://localhost:9000/v1", apiKey: "your-api-key" });

const transcript = await client.audio.transcriptions.create({
  model: "whisper-1",
  file: fs.createReadStream("audio.mp3"),
});
console.log(transcript.text);
</code></pre> <pre><code>curl http://localhost:9000/v1/audio/transcriptions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer your-api-key" \
  -F model=whisper-1 \
  -F file=@audio.mp3 \
  -F response_format=verbose_json \
  -F "timestamp_granularities[]=word"
</code></pre> <p>When <code>API_KEY</code> is not set, any API key is accepted; the OpenAI libraries require one, so pass any value.</p>
